# The configuration of the kube-scheduler of the k3s server. Three score plugins decide the node:
# - NodeResourcesFit with the strategy LeastAllocated gives the highest score to the node with the lowest requested
#   share of its allocatable CPU and memory. CPU and memory have the same weight, because either one can be the
#   resource that a site lacks.
# - NodeResourcesBalancedAllocation gives the highest score to the node whose requested CPU share and memory share are
#   nearest after the pod. A pod with much memory and little CPU therefore prefers a node with free memory and little
#   free CPU, and the reverse.
# - NodeAffinity with the weight 50 gives the highest score to the node of a preferred node affinity. The admission
#   policy of the site placement (../../../../cluster/placement-policy.yaml) gives each new pod of the stores and the
#   zones a preferred node affinity for its planned node (../../../../placement.py). 50 x 100 is above the sum of the
#   resource scores (2 x 10 x 100), so a pod starts on its planned node when that node has room. A pod without a
#   planned node, or whose planned node is full, goes to the node of the resource scores.
# The weight 10 is above the weights of the other score plugins (at most 3), so the requests decide the node of a pod
# without a plan, and a node that joins with no requests takes the new pods first. The other plugins keep their
# defaults.
# The allocatable CPU of a node counts threads of the fastest node (../../../../config.py kubelet_reserved()).
# A pod that started away from its planned node stays there. deploy-k3s up --rebalance moves running pods to their
# planned nodes (../../../../placement.py).
apiVersion: kubescheduler.config.k8s.io/v1
kind: KubeSchedulerConfiguration
clientConnection:
  kubeconfig: /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/cred/scheduler.kubeconfig
profiles:
  - schedulerName: default-scheduler
    plugins:
      score:
        enabled:
          - name: NodeResourcesFit
            weight: 10
          - name: NodeResourcesBalancedAllocation
            weight: 10
          - name: NodeAffinity
            weight: 50
    pluginConfig:
      - name: NodeResourcesFit
        args:
          scoringStrategy:
            type: LeastAllocated
            resources:
              - name: cpu
                weight: 1
              - name: memory
                weight: 1
      - name: NodeResourcesBalancedAllocation
        args:
          resources:
            - name: cpu
              weight: 1
            - name: memory
              weight: 1
